&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to shape the libraries developers use to build and run accelerator workloads? Apply to join Graphcore’s AI Compute Libraries team in Bristol.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 id=&quot;isPasted&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Metrea delivers effects-as-a-service to national security partners across five domains and more than a dozen mission areas. These include airborne ISR, electronic warfare, secure communications, aerial refueling, special air missions, aerial firefighting, and advanced simulation. We own the whole stack: designing, building, and operating turnkey capabilities that give our partners decisive, asymmetric advantage against rapidly evolving threats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our operating model is built around three interlocking pillars. The Support Groups provide a global shared-service – spanning people, finance, platform, operations, legal, and engagement. This frees up our Core Groups, who develop and own mission capabilities end-to-end, to focus entirely on delivery. The Market Groups apply a regional lens, ensuring that our agile and adaptable capabilities remain aligned to the wicked problems that matter most to our partners across the Americas, EMEA, and Asia-Pacific.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of our model is a simple but powerful idea: be a true partner with skin in the game. Our partners need effects, not just equipment. By owning the full stack – from the lab to the field – we are able to drive a continuous cycle of innovation that keeps our partners ahead. It&#39;s a fast-moving, intellectually demanding environment where talented people are given real responsibility, work on problems that matter, and contribute to an enterprise that is growing quickly and deliberately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Washington, DC, with facilities across the United States, the United Kingdom, as well as Continental Europe and Asia-Pacific.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Group&amp;nbsp;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Electromagnetic and Cyber Group (EM&amp;amp;C) is responsible for developing flexible and survivable advanced electronic warfare and secure communications equipment while providing the industry’s leading signals intelligence, electronic warfare, and cyber experts.  Metrea specialises in signal classification, direction finding, advanced geolocation techniques, and waveform development including waveforms for MANET and LPI/LPD applications. Metrea also develops special purpose radios for government customers and licenses DF and geolocation solutions to multiple OEMs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt;The Expeditionary Operations Lab, or EXOLAB, focuses on the rapid development, integration, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt;evaluation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt; and delivery of expeditionary capabilities within the Electromagnetic Warfare and Cyber domain.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt;EXOLAB works across research and development, experimentation, prototyping, systems integration, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt;trials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt; and operational delivery. The team addresses complex customer problems by combining existing technologies, emerging &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt;capabilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt; and internally developed solutions into deployable systems.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt;The lab &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt;operates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt; across airborne, land, maritime and dismounted environments, with a strong emphasis on practical engineering, rapid learning and delivering systems that are operationally relevant, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt;supportable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot;&gt; and resilient.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP Selected SCXW239653401 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Principal RF Engineer to lead and support the research, design, development, integration and delivery of radio-frequency systems for expeditionary Electronic Warfare, signals intelligence, spectrum operations and secure communications capabilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will be responsible for the RF engineering aspects of prototype and operational systems, including RF architecture, receiver and transmitter chains, antenna systems, signal distribution, filtering, amplification, frequency conversion, interference management and system performance analysis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Principal RF Engineer will operate as a senior technical authority within a multidisciplinary team comprising electrical, systems, mechanical, software, cyber and operational specialists. The role will support the full engineering lifecycle, from concept development and technology evaluation through detailed design, integration, verification, trials, deployment and through-life support.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a practical, delivery-focused engineering role. The successful candidate will be comfortable moving between theoretical analysis, simulation, laboratory testing, prototype development, platform integration and field trials.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will be based either in Lincoln or London, with a longer-term intent to transition the primary location to London if hired initially in Lincoln.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Design, develop and integrate RF systems for expeditionary Unmanned Systems control, Electronic Warfare, signals intelligence, spectrum-monitoring and secure communications capabilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Develop RF system architectures covering antennas, receivers, transmitters, amplifiers, filters, frequency conversion, switching and signal distribution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Conduct RF performance analysis, including gain, noise figure, sensitivity, dynamic range, linearity, link budgets and interference assessments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Support rapid R&amp;amp;D, prototyping and technology evaluation, translating operational requirements into practical and deployable RF solutions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Integrate commercial, government and internally developed RF equipment across airborne, vehicle-mounted, maritime, fixed-site and unmanned platforms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Plan and conduct RF testing, characterisation, fault diagnosis, verification and corrective engineering activity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Ensure RF designs consider electromagnetic compatibility, spectrum management, grounding, bonding, shielding, environmental protection and relevant standards&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Work closely with electrical, mechanical, software, cyber, systems and operational teammates throughout the engineering lifecycle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Support UK and international trials, demonstrations, installations, commissioning and operational deployments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Provide RF technical leadership, design assurance and clear engineering recommendations to customers, suppliers and internal stakeholders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
